  "job": "Pours resin under the enemy front line; whoever is still standing in it when it sets is stuck.",
  "difficulty": 2,
  "lore": "Odrum tends the resin pans that feed the lamps of the east rim, and he learned early that warm lampresin goes where you pour it and stays where it sets. He carries two pots on a walnut yoke and a sling that doubles as a ladle. Serenade cooks complain that he talks about resin at dinner; Aubade runners complain that their boots are still stuck to the Noonline. He is patient in the way of people who wait for things to harden, and he has never once hurried a shot.",
